      ":question/id": "0218f572-6ced-52c5-be27-fc7cde79cda8",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -6 & 0 \\\\ -11 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -5 & -5 & -1 \\\\ 10 & 11 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
