  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186119772,
      "id": "b55b50a0-034f-57c0-8a61-883cfb0412dc",
      "title": "Identifying a Triangular Matrix"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "25a48f29-ea91-546d-8745-d56c3129fda9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 8 & -11 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ab31aac8-8a8e-5800-b02d-3eb29cdcdaaa",
