    "question": {
      ":question/id": "8e9b8f68-d41d-5e39-bf5c-fc7872ec41b9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -10 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -11 & 10 & -4 \\\\ -7 & -7 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a7aad1c3-5fe6-5a6c-b761-e3e52b03e0a8",
