    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b7082407-642c-5e8c-908f-d8dccd3869c2",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $B$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & -9 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 10 & 8 \\\\ 10 & -9 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
