    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2d221056-af51-5ecc-85aa-ebfede7934a9",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 11 \\\\ -10 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "205f056e-8bd7-56cd-981a-653a69607270",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
