      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $C$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 \\\\ -7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -10 \\\\ 6 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
