    "question": {
      ":question/id": "514b43da-0b12-59fc-89cc-cdcd614cdabb",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 6 & -11 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "63559aa6-c3d4-57ad-9fb4-244430084626",
