    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5b10b2bb-4ddb-502d-9cbc-a9ba9f0ebce6",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $E$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 7 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "bef7d8dc-23a8-5515-b250-ac5b935aaa6c",
