    "question": {
      ":question/id": "35c6f50a-4a31-5adf-a5aa-d5e61a033e4f",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $D$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -11 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -3 \\\\ 11 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -11 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
