      ":question/id": "0851cc8a-9b2d-5c8f-87c2-b95fb5de42cc",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 11 & 10 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -11 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 \\\\ -10 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
